    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nMotions always occur in pairs:\n\n- `j` & `k`\n- `w` & `b`\n- `e` & `ge`\n- `/...<cr>` & `?...<cr>`\n\nTherefore, when CmdAtom detects a motion, it should provide information about the corresponding motion, e.g.\n\nThe current `event.data` is\n\n```lua\n  data = {\n    changed = false,\n    cmd = \"j\",\n    keys = \"j\",\n    lhs = \"j\",\n    moved = true,\n    pos = { 9, 15 },\n    type = \"motion\",\n    undoseq = 117\n  },\n```\n\n\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nbut I would like it to be\n\n```lua\n  data = {\n    changed = false,\n    cmd = \"j\",\n    keys = \"j\",\n    lhs = \"j\",\n    motion_type = \"forward\",\n    paired_motion = {\n        cmd = \"k\",\n        keys = \"k\",\n        lhs = \"k\",\n        motion_type = \"backward\",\n    },\n    moved = true,\n    pos = { 9, 15 },\n    type = \"motion\",\n    undoseq = 117\n  },\n```\n\nThis would make it possible to bind two keys to repeat motions in both directions. for example, `,` to repeat the motion in the \"backward\" direction and `;` to repeat it in the \"forward\" direction.\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
